-- Matcha LuaVM: FurryHook (draggable + transparent UI, compact text Hotbar)
-- OPTIMIZED BUILD (local-register fix)
-- Notes:
--  * FIX: Lua/Luau allows max 200 locals alive in one function. The whole script
--    used to live in one top-level chunk and went over that limit
--    ("Out of local registers ... exceeded limit 200"). Every feature section
--    below is now wrapped in its own `do ... end` block so its locals go out of
--    scope when the block ends. Only shared helpers stay at the top level.
--    Blocks report their load state through the STATUS table.
--    RULE: if you add features, wrap them in a `do ... end` block too.
--  * UI.AddTab's callback runs every frame, so it only reads pre-built data
--    (no closures / string building inside it).
--  * Username and the Players folder are resolved once and cached.
--  * A feature does no work while its toggle is off.
--  * Every panel (Player Info, Inv Aim, Staff List, Hotbar, Server Loot) is draggable
--    by its top bar and uses the "UI Opacity" slider. Notifications are NOT affected.
--  * Nothing prints to the console except one line at the very end (only if
--    everything loaded without a problem) and ONE warning if a loop hits an error.
--  * Performance: the Server Loot scan is spread out (one player per tick, big
--    inventories sliced across frames), dragging only moves visible drawings,
--    and instance lookups (reports, HRPs, hotbar folder) are cached.

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
